# The built prototype is a deliverable, not source.
#
# dist-spa holds the whole product inlined into one self-contained file, which
# is committed on purpose: a judge can download it and open the entire thing
# with no server. But at 1.6 MB apiece the two builds are more than twice the
# byte weight of the actual codebase, and GitHub measures languages in bytes —
# so the repository was being labelled an HTML project written in TypeScript.
#
# Marking them generated keeps the files, drops them from the language stats,
# and collapses them in diffs, where a 1.6 MB minified blob is pure noise.
dist-spa/** linguist-generated=true
